! GAPS corpus-coverage deck (family=modes): HARMONICMODE with DoAllHarmonics=No
! (Pascal TSolutionAlgs.SolveHarmonic, SolutionAlgs.pas:1011). The existing
! harmonics decks (isource_harm, reactor_rlcurve) only exercise the collected-
! frequency path (DoAllHarmonics=Yes). Here `Set harmonics=(1 3 5 13)` takes the
! EXPLICIT-LIST branch (set_cmd.rs:443, do_all_harmonics=false), and isolates two
! more sub-branches in one sweep:
!  * h=1 -> the `Abs(Harmonic-1.0)>EPSILON` skip-fundamental gate +
!    RetrieveSavedVoltages (last solve was the fundamental snapshot);
!  * h=13 -> a frequency ABSENT from every spectrum (sp5 tops out at 11) -> a
!    zero-injection SolveDirect at 780 Hz.
! Feature-sensitive: dropping h=13 from the list (or switching to harmonics=ALL)
! changes the swept monitor sample set — proven on the oracle.
Clear
New Circuit.gaps_hlist basekv=12.47 phases=3 bus1=sourcebus mvasc3=200 mvasc1=210
New Spectrum.sp5 numharm=5 harmonic=(1 3 5 7 11) %mag=(100 18 12 8 5) angle=(0 0 0 0 0)
New Line.l1 bus1=sourcebus bus2=b1 phases=3 r1=0.30 x1=0.90 r0=0.9 x0=2.7 c1=3.0 c0=1.5 length=2 units=km
New Line.l2 bus1=b1 bus2=b2 phases=3 r1=0.35 x1=0.95 r0=1.0 x0=2.8 c1=3.0 c0=1.5 length=1.5 units=km
New Load.ld1 bus1=b1 phases=3 kv=12.47 kw=700 pf=0.95 model=1 spectrum=sp5
New Isource.ih bus1=b2 phases=3 amps=8 angle=0 spectrum=sp5
New Monitor.m_h element=Line.l2 terminal=1 mode=0
Set voltagebases=[12.47]
Calcvoltagebases
Solve
! Explicit harmonic list (DoAllHarmonics off); h=13 is absent from sp5.
Set harmonics=(1 3 5 13)
Set mode=harmonics
Solve
